    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n“Carrick” is a unique, architect designed, detached contemporary residence. Extending to an impressive 515 sq. m. (5,543 sq. ft.), this outstanding six-bedroom, six-bathroom home is accessed via electric vehicular gates and offers absolute privacy. The property includes a spacious two car garage and additional off-street parking.\n\nBuilt circa 2006, sustainable luxury is at the core of this B1-rated home. The layout is meticulously inverted to maximise natural light and elevated views. A 6-person internal lift connects all three floors. \n\n“Carrick” exudes understated elegance with striking proportions, light-filled accommodation, quality craftsmanship and superb design. The welcoming entrance hallway leads into a large recreation /home cinema room and a guest wc. This floor also features two spacious double bedrooms, both complete with luxury en-suite bathrooms. A stunning hand-crafted, oak and glass staircase and a discreetly integrated lift complete this floor. \n\nGenerous functional accommodation continues the first floor which hosts four spacious bedrooms and four bathrooms. The same uncompromising standard showcases custom crafted wardrobes and luxury bathroom units. The master suite benefits from a walk-in wardrobe, dressing room, and direct garden access. \n\nThe top floor is stunning with breathtaking elevated views towards the Dodder River. There is an open plan expansive kitchen, complete with spacious dining area, and an elevated lounge at mezzanine level. A spacious, light-filled living room and a utility room are also found at this level. \n\nThe property transitions seamlessly from its upper floor to the outdoors with a wraparound balcony to the front, a private South-facing terrace and a South-Westerly facing garden. The unique artistic design of the building is interwoven into the fabric of the terrace and lawned garden, showcasing two original commissioned stone sculptures by acclaimed Irish artist Remco de Fouw. \n\nWithin walking distance of both Terenure and Rathfarnham villages, “Carrick” offers immediate access to artisan cafes, boutique shopping, and premium dining. The property is moments from Bushy Park and the River Dodder Greenway. Dublin's most prestigious primary and secondary schools are within easy reach as are a host of premium sporting clubs. The area is exceptionally well serviced by buses to Dublin Airport, city centre, and third level colleges. There is ease of access to the M50 motorway located just minutes away. \n\nFrom its robust foundations to the striking patina copper ringed roof, this home seamlessly blends bold architectural design with sustainable luxury. “Carrick” offers a rare opportunity to acquire a residence of distinction in a much sought after location."
      },
